A||N||7||MikeSchaefer||Value of 88 Formula, 20k miles??||||5||
Z||000000||MikeSchaefer||06-20-2001||05:31 PM||||A friend of mine picked up a white 88 Formula (all options except PM, has sunroof) with 20k miles on it last week and is looking for it's value.  It was hit on the front passenger side wheel area pretty hard, but could be fixed for around $2000 (approx).  He's been wanting to know whether this car should be parted out or fixed, what would you guys think it's worth?  It is showroom condition besides the damage, which is mostly frame work and repainting a couple of panels.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Mike Schaefer||||reg||5
Z||000001||Formula88||06-20-2001||05:44 PM||||All depends on the frame work.  If it can be fixed, it's definately worth it.  Low mileage Formulas in good shape are hard to come by!||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||06-20-2001||06:13 PM||||Values are really a subjective thing, but generally speaking, a 20K mile Formula (with no issues) would be "worth" about $6000-$7000.  It sounds like it is loaded, as far as Formulas go (pm weren't an option), so it'll be in that ballpark.  Of course, since it was wrecked then repaired some "value" is taken away.  You couldn't compare it to another 20K mile Formula that hasn't been damaged.<BR> <BR>If it can be competently repaired for $2000 then I would do it.  Of course it depends on what your friend paid for it too. If he got it for a song, then it's worth sinking the $$ into it, but if he paid a lot then it might be more worthwhile to part it out to recoup some investment.<P>I hope it's salvageable myself.<BR>There's nothing worse than parting out a good fixable car.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||KissMySSFiero||06-20-2001||06:33 PM||||how much did he pay for it?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Toddster||06-20-2001||07:44 PM||||I bought a formula in the wrecking yard two years ago with frame damage. Me and some friends stripped the miscellaneous parts off and delivered the car with just a few panels (for alignment purposes). We roled it up onto the frame straightening rack. $600 later, I had a straight frame.<P>It was worth it to me.||||reg||1
Z||000005||MikeSchaefer||06-20-2001||08:15 PM||||He paid $400 for it (I almost killed him when I heard that), I imagine the value would be around $6000 or so once it's fixed, but do you think it would be easy for him to sell?  He wants to purchase a fastback with the money he brings in for it.<BR>Thanks again,<BR>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000006||Urchin||06-20-2001||08:35 PM||||Well then after he fixes it he can sell it to me!!  I'm selling my existing fiero and holding out for a formula.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature2_3.jpg">   <P>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fformula88||06-20-2001||11:09 PM||||That car fixed would go for a good amount.  Any low milage 88 V6 Fiero will go for a good $$.  Of course, if he doesn't want to go thru the trouble of fixing it I'll be glad to take it off his hands!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  ||||reg||1
